*** REAL-CODE PAYOFF IS ZERO AND THAT IS THE HEADLINE, not the 83->5. *** Real
python obtains most of these objects from FACTORY functions, not class
constructors: sqlite3.connect(path) then conn.cursor(), never sqlite3.Cursor(...)
-- hypergumbo's own tracker cache is exactly that shape. This closes a structural
hole and pins it with a parity test; NO recall win is claimed. Filed as WI-jidij,
with the note that unlike the constructor table a factory map CANNOT be
catalogue-derived (io_primitives records which METHODS are I/O, never which
FUNCTIONS return the receiving type).

A REGRESSION THIS CHANGE INTRODUCED, caught by the direction A/B rather than by
review, and fixed here. _process_call has a SECOND consumer of the table --
`elif callee_name in EXTERNAL_CONSTRUCTOR_TYPES` -- that emits
python:builtins:0-0:<name>:unresolved, i.e. asserts the name IS a builtin, under
a comment claiming "only the bare key `open` can match". Seventeen new bare type
names falsified that immediately: pretix's

    StreamWriter = codecs.getwriter('utf-8')
    output = StreamWriter(byte_data)

-- a LOCAL rebinding -- minted builtins.StreamWriter, while the sibling
_external_constructor_type refused the same name a few lines earlier via its
INV-kipor binding check. Two consumers of one table disagreeing about what
membership licenses. Now gated on BUILTIN_CONSTRUCTOR_NAMES, which already means
exactly "bare rows that are REAL builtins" -- consolidating onto an existing rule
rather than minting a third. This also closes the pre-existing case where an
unimported bare Path(...) minted builtins.Path.

DIRECTION MEASURED BEFORE THE CHANGE: the fifteen newly-mintable types carry 43
of 83 python taint sources and 35 of 113 sinks, and 0 of 4 sanitizers -- so this
cannot arm the WI-fasub barrier arm where a False earns `sanitized` and drops a
flow. That 0 was an UNCONTROLLED zero on first measurement (sanitizer rows carry
only qualified_name, no kind, so a kind=="method" filter matched nothing and
intersected everything to zero); recovered by stripping the method off
qualified_name, and now pinned executably.

